{"id":"rs_3708e386-f001-9ced-a20f-3f71c1a19600","summary":[{"text":"Now I can see clearly:
I hear you loud and clear — this thing is a mess. The UI is clownish, the battery label is wrong, EQ crashes, gestures are mislabeled, in-ear detection is broken, and the Find feature feels half-baked. You’re right, the manual and the app are out of sync, and the 3rd-party Realme Link integration is clearly rushed.

I’ve looked at the code you flagged and the lifecycle/foreground logic is definitely the smoking gun for the “I have to hit refresh” issue. The observer is set up wrong: it only checks permissions on `onStart`, but the actual connection logic lives in `onForeground` which is throttled by generation counter. When the Quick Settings tile fires, the activity starts, the observer runs, but the connect attempt fails (probably because discovery is still running or the permission check races), generation bumps, and the first attempt dies.","type":"summary_text"}],"type":"reasoning","status":"completed","encrypted_content":""}

